rule.description:
@IsTest methods must prove behaviour with meaningful assertions.
This rule flags four coverage-theatre patterns:

1. A test method with zero Assert.* calls — coverage without
   verification.
2. catch(Exception error) {} — swallows exceptions silently.
   Use Assert.fail('Should throw ...') + Assert.isInstanceOfType.
3. Boolean exceptionThrown = false; try { ... }
   catch(Exception error) { exceptionThrown = true; }
   Explicitly forbidden by docs/Code Conventions - Guide.md.
4. Assert.isNotNull(record) immediately after
   (SObject)TST_Builder.of(...).build(). TST_Builder.build()
   throws if insertion fails, so the non-null assertion adds
   no coverage. Assert on defaults or derived fields instead.

Example of non-compliant code:

Boolean exceptionThrown = false;
try { doSomething(); }
catch(Exception error) { exceptionThrown = true; }
Assert.isTrue(exceptionThrown, 'should throw');

Example of compliant code:

try
{
   doSomething();
   Assert.fail('Expected IllegalArgumentException');
}
catch(Exception error)
{
   Assert.isInstanceOfType(error, IllegalArgumentException.class, 'Incorrect type');
}

property.value:
(: Pattern 1 — @IsTest methods with zero assertion-shaped calls. :)
(: Recognises Assert.* plus any helper whose method name starts with :)
(: 'assert' (e.g. assertServiceCompleted, assertCallSuccessful). :)
//Method[
   ModifierNode/Annotation[lower-case(@Name) = 'istest']
   and not(.//MethodCallExpression[
      starts-with(lower-case(@FullMethodName), 'assert.')
      or starts-with(lower-case(@MethodName), 'assert')
   ])
]
|
(: Pattern 2 — empty catch block inside an @IsTest method. :)
//Method[ModifierNode/Annotation[lower-case(@Name) = 'istest']]
   //CatchBlockStatement[not(BlockStatement/*)]
|
(: Pattern 3 — exception-sentinel anti-pattern: a local assigned inside a catch :)
(: of a try that carries no Assert.fail/throw does the job Assert.fail must do :)
(: (Boolean flag, captured Exception, inverse Assert.isNull); the classic :)
(: 'Boolean exceptionThrown' name fires regardless. Same predicate as :)
(: KernNoBooleanExceptionThrown — keep the two in step. :)
//Method[ModifierNode/Annotation[lower-case(@Name) = 'istest']]
   //VariableDeclaration[
      (lower-case(@Type) = 'boolean' and lower-case(@Image) = 'exceptionthrown')
      or
      (
         not(ancestor::CatchBlockStatement)
         and @Image = ancestor::Method[1]
               //TryCatchFinallyBlockStatement[
                  not(BlockStatement[1]//MethodCallExpression[ends-with(lower-case(@FullMethodName), 'assert.fail')])
                  and not(BlockStatement[1]//ThrowStatement)
               ]
               /CatchBlockStatement//AssignmentExpression/VariableExpression[1]/@Image
      )
   ]
|
(: Pattern 4 — Assert.isNotNull(var) where var was declared from :)
(: (SObject)TST_Builder.of(...).build() in the preceding statement. The :)
(: sibling step runs from the ExpressionStatement, not the call inside it, :)
(: which has no siblings. :)
//Method[ModifierNode/Annotation[lower-case(@Name) = 'istest']]
   //ExpressionStatement[
      MethodCallExpression[
         lower-case(@FullMethodName) = 'assert.isnotnull'
         and VariableExpression[1]/@Image =
            ../preceding-sibling::*[1][self::VariableDeclarationStatements]
               /VariableDeclaration[
                  .//MethodCallExpression[@MethodName = 'build']
                  and .//ReferenceExpression[@Image = 'TST_Builder']
               ]/@Image
      ]
   ]

rule.description:
The exception-sentinel family is forbidden by docs/Code Conventions - Guide.md
(Exception testing). Every member relies on a local declared before the try and
assigned inside a catch to detect that the call threw, so the test never says what
it expected, loses the exception type, and skips the original error message:

Boolean exceptionThrown = false;   /  Boolean threw = false;
Exception caught;                  /  DmlException caught;
try { doSomething(); }
catch(Exception error) { exceptionThrown = true; }   /  { caught = error; }
Assert.isTrue(exceptionThrown, ...);  /  Assert.isNotNull(caught, ...);

The inverse sentinel is forbidden for the same reason: 'Exception caught; try { ... }
catch(Exception error) { caught = error; } Assert.isNull(caught, ...)' swallows the
real failure. A test that must NOT throw simply calls the method with no try/catch;
if it throws, the test fails with the real error and stack.

Use the canonical Apex pattern:

try
{
   doSomething();
   Assert.fail('Expected IllegalArgumentException');
}
catch(Exception error)
{
   Assert.isInstanceOfType(error, IllegalArgumentException.class, 'Incorrect type');
}

The rule fires on any local in an @IsTest method that is assigned inside a catch of
a try whose body carries neither Assert.fail nor a throw — the variable is doing the
job Assert.fail must do. The classic 'Boolean exceptionThrown' name fires regardless.

property.value:
//Method[ModifierNode/Annotation[lower-case(@Name) = 'istest']]
   //VariableDeclaration[
      (lower-case(@Type) = 'boolean' and lower-case(@Image) = 'exceptionthrown')
      or
      (
         not(ancestor::CatchBlockStatement)
         and @Image = ancestor::Method[1]
               //TryCatchFinallyBlockStatement[
                  not(BlockStatement[1]//MethodCallExpression[ends-with(lower-case(@FullMethodName), 'assert.fail')])
                  and not(BlockStatement[1]//ThrowStatement)
               ]
               /CatchBlockStatement//AssignmentExpression/VariableExpression[1]/@Image
      )
   ]

rule.description:
Coverage-theatre suppressions are high-impact and must be
reviewed. This rule flags every @SuppressWarnings that contains
PMD.KernNoCoverageTheatre (case-insensitive) so reviewers can
confirm the adjacent justification comment exists and is
substantive (not placeholders like "tricky", "todo", "fixme",
"hard to test", or "hack").

Prefer narrowing suppression to the single method that needs
it. Class-level suppressions hide intent across the whole file.

Example (flagged — always requires review):

@SuppressWarnings('PMD.KernNoCoverageTheatre')
private static void shouldEmitEvent() { ... }

Example (compliant — reviewer confirms justification comment):

// Platform event delivery is async; Test.stopTest + CURRENT_RUN
// query is the only verification available.
@SuppressWarnings('PMD.KernNoCoverageTheatre')
private static void shouldEmitPlatformEvent() { ... }

property.value:
//Annotation[
   lower-case(@Name) = 'suppresswarnings'
   and .//AnnotationParameter[
      contains(
         translate(string(@Value), 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ', 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'),
         'pmd.kernnocoveragetheatre'
      )
      or contains(
         translate(string(@Image), 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ', 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'),
         'pmd.kernnocoveragetheatre'
      )
   ]
]
